  "details": "Using Custom Tags on any `GameObject` may invalidate all references to its entire hierarchy tree, starting at the first parent, including all siblings, and all children.\n\nI used Custom Tags, and they worked fine until I used the Tag `17`.\n\n1. Create multiple Custom Tags to create one with Index `17`.\n\n2. Assign Custom Tag to any `GameObject`.\n\n3. Access or reference this `GameObject` from an `UdonBehaviour` with the `Untagged` Tag that's part of a different Root `GameObject`.\n\nThe `UdonBehaviour` will have all references to this `GameObject` with Tag `17` set to `null`.\n\nThe expected Behaviour is, that VRChat, which is not uploading Custom Tags anyway, shouldn't upload Tag Indexes/Values in the first place. Instead, they should replace all Custom Tags with `Untagged`.\n\nMy suggested solution for everyone else who is encountering this, make an Editor Tool/Script that sets all your Custom Tags to `Untagged` after handling them.",
